{"id":"20260826T001246.310656882Z-e6faf310","time":"2026-08-26T00:12:46.310656882Z","session_id":"session-20260826T001004.582107347Z","task_id":"task-1787703004582360212","source":"system","kind":"status","summary":"Authority for this plan, by lane.\n\nrequested objective:\n  A task interrupted after its plan was authorised cannot be resumed: nothing reconstructs, from the recorded event stream, which tasks were left in that state.\n\nAdd to internal/session the exported type and function:\n\n    type Interrupted struct { TaskID, Task, Plan, Review string }\n    func FindInterrupted(events []event.Event) []Interrupted\n\nGiven a session's events it returns one entry per task that was created, had its authority RESOLVED, and never reached a terminal workflow outcome -- carrying the task text, the plan, and the reviewer's latest status if one exists. A plan that was merely PROPOSED is not resumable: a task still waiting on a human has produced no work to continue. Tasks that completed or failed are excluded, entries come back in the order the tasks first appeared, and a task with no recorded request text is not returned.\n  NOT established as a human objective — submitted unattended; no human presence was established\n  the wording is the task; it is not a person's authorization for it\n\ntechnical claims:\n  [evidence-bearing] Sensei classifies this scoped change as architecture-sensitive with local blast radius and identifies two critical authority and resume invariants. (internal/session/store.go and internal/session/interrupted_test.go) — source: graph\n  [evidence-bearing] Store.Load returns events in their recorded JSONL order. (internal/session/store.go) — source: repository\n  [evidence-bearing] The workflow records request text in TaskCreated summaries, rendered plans in PlanProposed summaries, and explicit human choices as AuthorityResolved events. (internal/workflow/engine.go) — source: repository\n  [evidence-bearing] Reviewer decisions are recorded as SourceReviewer Status events, while successful and failed terminal outcomes use WorkflowCompleted and WorkflowFailed. (internal/workflow/engine.go and internal/event/event.go) — source: repository\n  [evidence-bearing] Sensei links the resume invariant to behavioral tests for excluding unapproved and finished tasks. (internal/session/interrupted_test.go) — source: graph\n  the objective does not establish any of these. Evidence does.\n\nconsequence decision:\n  BOUNDED — the candidate worktree: files are edited in an isolated checkout, the diff is audited before it leaves, and discarding the worktree leaves the world unchanged\n  assessed from the action, not from who asked and not from whether the plan satisfies the objective.\n\nrouted: human-authority-required\n"}
